From 9e2795869d9588ee60cb11103164f3610a4a3aa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen De Vleeschauwer <kdv@kdvelectronics.eu>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:17:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] swo: Add DWT trace decoding and the mon dwt command

Backport of DWT tracing from blackmagic-rtthread (9ab30842, cortexm
command registration from f8a58382) to the firmware.

- mon dwt configures the target's DWT/ITM/TPIU for trace over SWO:
  [enable|disable|status|clear|0..31|exception|event|lts <0..3>|
  gts <0..3>|timestamp]...
- The ITM decoder (swo_dwt_itm_decode.c) replaces
  stm32/swo_itm_decode.c with the same API; besides ITM stimulus it
  decodes DWT PC samples, exception trace, event counters, data trace
  and timestamps.
- mon swo gains log, top and graph (a PC sample histogram over an
  address range) and selftest (replays known packets through the
  decoder, no target needed).

Firmware specific changes:
- Dropped the RT-Thread code (rt_calloc/rt_free, CherryUSB buffer size)
  and kept swo.h's !NO_LIBOPENCM3 guard as upstream has it.
- Kept the "Trace enabled for BMP serial ..., USB EP ..." line, which
  host tools parse.
- Adapted to upstream's PLATFORM_HAS_SWO rename.
- newlib-nano's integer printf has no %zu: the self-test used it, which
  made %s dereference a small integer and fault. Use PRIu32 instead.
- Pace the self-test report, as debug_serial_send_stdout() drops data
  while the previous USB packet is pending.
- Replaced a GNU case range with an if.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
